body:
Type-annotated `let` bindings currently fail with:

```
:sir
:siret
let v: Int = 0
v
//│ FAILURE: Unexpected compilation error
//│ FAILURE LOCATION: go (Elaborator.scala:1907)
//│ ╔══[COMPILATION ERROR] Unsupported let binding shape
//│ ║  l.13: 	let v: Int = 0
//│ ╙──      	    ^^^^^^^^^^
//│ FAILURE: Unexpected compilation error
//│ FAILURE LOCATION: subterm (Elaborator.scala:1197)
//│ ╔══[COMPILATION ERROR] Name not found: v
//│ ║  l.14: 	v
//│ ╙──      	^
```

It currently elaborates patterns using a separate, incomplete procedure:
```fs
case 0 | 1
//│ FAILURE: Unexpected compilation error
//│ FAILURE LOCATION: patternBranch (SplitElaborator.scala:247)
//│ ╔══[COMPILATION ERROR] Unrecognized pattern split (operator application).
//│ ║  l.12:   case 0 | 1
//│ ╙──             ^^^^^
//│ = fun
```

UCS patterns are compiled fine:

```fs
data class Add(val lhs, val rhs)

:sjs
case Add(0, 0) then 1
//│ ————————————| JS (unsanitized) |————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
//│ let lambda;
//│ lambda = (undefined, function (caseScrut) {
//│   let arg$Add$0$, arg$Add$1$;
//│   if (caseScrut instanceof Add1.class) {
//│     arg$Add$0$ = caseScrut.lhs;
//│     arg$Add$1$ = caseScrut.rhs;
//│     if (arg$Add$0$ === 0) {
//│       if (arg$Add$1$ === 0) {
//│         return 1
//│       }
//│       throw globalThis.Object.freeze(new globalThis.Error("match error"));
//│     }
//│     throw globalThis.Object.freeze(new globalThis.Error("match error"));
//│   }
//│   throw globalThis.Object.freeze(new globalThis.Error("match error"));
//│ });
//│ return lambda
//│ —————————————————| Output |—————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
//│ = fun
```

